e0106_hidden_result_regions  defect  2  ADR 0028 — E0106 does not see a HIDDEN result region
    # 2026-09-22 — the E0106 rule fires when the return type carries an elided
    # REFERENCE region (`&T`, `&[T]`, `&dyn Tr`) with more than one input region and
    # no `&self`. It does NOT fire when the result's region is HIDDEN: a
    # `#[borrow_carrying]` ADT that declares no region parameter (`RtVal`, `WAny`).
    # Those signatures are equally ambiguous and Rust refuses them too.
    # LIVE CONSEQUENCE: `pub type QFn = fn(&[RtVal]) -> RtVal;` — Rust spells it
    # `fn(&'x [RtVal<'s>]) -> RtVal<'s>`, the result comes from the VALUES and never
    # from the borrow of the buffer. With both elided the hidden-result rule takes
    # every elided input, so `eval_sexpr`'s `f(&argv[..])` read as returning a borrow
    # of the local `argv`. That call site is laundered through `slice_from_raw` with
    # `unsafe` as the honest marker — a scaffold, not the answer.
    # ⚠ BLOCKED ON A SEPARATE DEFECT. Giving `RtVal` a region parameter was tried and
    # made it WORSE: an ADT with a declared region AND a loan-carrying payload lays out
    # a DIFFERENT NUMBER of regions as a declaration than as a mono instance, so
    # `labels()` and `walk_type()` disagree on the same type (measured:
    # `ret=RtVal decl=RtVal dest=RtVal lret=1 dst=2`, and elsewhere `lret=2 dst=1`)
    # and every call through it falls back to "?", which matches every source.
    # ORDER: align an ADT's region LAYOUT between declaration and instance; then
    # E0106 over hidden result regions; then `QFn` names its two and the laundering
    # in stdlib/mem/deem/tpl.logos comes out.

